 {"id":"RELEASE-2026-09-23-05","title":"[P2 RELEASE RISK] BT-042: ~/.local/bin/boardctl is a dirty from-HEAD build (79a1012, dirty=true) reporting version dev — no install target, no drift probe, stale since 2026-09-20","status":"pending","priority":"P2","type":"finding","created_at":"2026-09-09-21T13:07:00Z","created_by":"releng-sat","reasoning":"Measured 2026-09-21 and confirmed 2026-09-23: ~/.local/bin/boardctl mtime 2026-09-20 01:08; go version -m reports mod v0.1.7-0.20260920060733-79a10123addd+dirty, vcs.modified=true; version --json -> {version:dev,build:dev}. 79a1012 is the DF-BOARDCTL-2 merge and is NOT an ancestor of DF-BOARDCTL-6 (6189838); the installed copy lacks the newest user-facing fix and carries none of BT-039. Impact: any caller using PATH boardctl runs a stale, unreproducible binary with no identity. Containment: foreman skill already routes to ./bin/boardctl. Required: install target or documented install-by-tag step + sha256 verify in README/Development so drift is detectable at any time. Evidence: BT-042 pending on this board.","detail":{}}
 {"id": "BT-049", "title": "validate warns on bare ci_result \"PASS\" \u2014 per-field vocab check but union-format message makes in-union values look rejected", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "created_at": "2026-09-23T01:22:05", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T01:22:05", "description": null, "labels": null, "worker_status": "pending", "foreman_note": null, "reasoning": "validate.go:132-146 checks guard_result against {PASS,FAIL,SKIP} and ci_result against {GREEN,RED,SKIP} but formats BOTH warnings with the same union text '{PASS,FAIL,SKIP} / {GREEN,RED,SKIP}'. A bare ci_result \"PASS\" is IN the union but NOT in the ci vocabulary, so boards carrying bare PASS in ci_result get warned as free-form even though the value the warning itself advertises. 11 live rows on hermes-canopy (lines 170,171,173,175,176,179,180,182,183,184 of tasks.jsonl at 8c16e42a, incl. GAP-034/GAP-035) warn on exactly 'PASS' while bare GREEN never warns. Review #14 item 78 read the warning text as 'in-vocabulary value rejected'; the union-format message is what makes the per-field split invisible. Either accept PASS in ci_result (if PASS is legal there, make it so in CIResultVocabulary) or print the field's own vocabulary per field. Repro: 3-row board with ci_result PASS/GREEN/'judge PASS x' -> PASS warns, GREEN does not. boardctl validate (installed 10522390-byte binary, Sep 20).", "complexity": 3, "detail": {"fingerprint": "715de0410f6e60034303b53d7ca8916afa03b0eebe09fbbe74aac1a7da916314"}}
 {"id":"BT-050","title":"Board writers append rows directly instead of using boardctl create, so its guards (id refusal, shape) never run","status":"pending","priority":"P2","type":null,"created_at":"2026-09-23T06:45:50.227067+00:00","created_by":null,"reasoning":"Board writers append rows to tasks.jsonl directly instead of going through `boardctl create`, so the tool's own guards never run\n\nEVIDENCE (2026-09-23): hermes-canopy tick 557 (commit 854b21cc, \"DF-50/51/52 wave merged\") wrote TWO different findings under the same id DF-HERMES-CANOPY-52. The board then FAILED its own validator: `[error] tasks.jsonl line 386: duplicate task id \"DF-HERMES-CANOPY-52\" (also line 382)` -> RESULT: FAIL (1 error, 35 warnings), exit 1. Repair was a renumber to DF-HERMES-CANOPY-56 with provenance in review_notes (commit d6f38341), 386 rows in and out.\n\nROOT CAUSE: `boardctl create` already REFUSES an id that exists (exit 2, \"a re-detected finding is REFUSED\"), so the collision could not have happened through the tool. The writers - foreman ticks and worker skills - append with their own JSON serialisation, never calling it. The same bypass also explains the sibling defects seen this week: 84 distinct row shapes across 323 rows in gitreins (uniformity was never checked), the 35 free-form ci_result=\"PASS\" warnings on this very board, and the my-project 10-key rows against a 31-key canon.\n\nASK: make the direct-append path hard to reach and the tool path the obvious one - (a) a file lock so two concurrent writers cannot interleave, (b) flock-then-append as a first-class verb (or make `create` safe under concurrency), (c) extend validate to check KEY UNIFORMITY against a declared canon, not just ids/statuses/result vocabulary, and (d) make the foreman/worker skills mandate the verb rather than describing the JSON shape. Subgoal 70 of the review goal: \"we might want boardctl to get a task to prevent this type of problem and make sure all skills and agents modify boards via the tool and not direct\".\n\nSEEN IN: coding-hermes review programme, item 70 (heading duplicate ids) and the canopy board regression found 2026-09-23.","detail":{"fingerprint":"18320577634d8432ef35f704d5292b98c0d76cc3982eb7d8220984a59b215491"},"complexity":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-23T06:45:50.227067+00:00"}
